\title{Decode is bounded by the weight read}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786546736765}
\meta{anki-deck}{MLSys}

\prompt{200B parameters in bf16 across 32 TPU v4p. What is the lower bound on per-step sampling latency?}{
  ##{2\ \text{bytes} \times 200\mathrm{e}9 = 400\mathrm{e}9 \text{ bytes} \;\longrightarrow\; \frac{12.5\mathrm{e}9 \text{ bytes/chip}}{1.23\mathrm{e}12 \text{ B/s}} \approx 10\ \mathrm{ms}}

  It is a bound because every decode step has to re-read \em{all} the parameters from [HBM](AI2G) into the MXU, so no step can beat the weight-load time. At small batch it is close to achievable, too: decode is HBM-bandwidth-bound, not FLOPs-bound, which is the whole reason [batching pays](UZ6D).
}
